Rule 1 (input must be a 4-D tensor)
{input : tensor} |= ndim(input) = 4
>>
Rule 2 (size must be a 1-D tensor of 2 elements)
{size : tensor} |= ndim(size) = 1 ∧ shape(size, 0) = 2
>>
Rule 3 (offsets must be a 2-D tensor of shape [batch_size, 2], where batch_size is the first dimension of input)
{input : tensor, offsets : tensor} |= ndim(offsets) = 2 ∧ shape(offsets, 0) = shape(input, 0) ∧ shape(offsets, 1) = 2
>>
Rule 4 (noise must be one of the allowed strings)
{noise : str} |= noise = "uniform" ∨ noise = "gaussian" ∨ noise = "zero"
>>
Rule 5 (glimpse height and width must be positive)
{size : tensor} |= shape(size, 0) > 0 ∧ shape(size, 1) > 0
>>
Rule 6 (input and offsets should have compatible data types)
{input : tensor, offsets : tensor} |= dtype_(input) = 7 ∧ dtype_(offsets) = 7
>>
Rule 7 (size should have int32 datatype)
{size : tensor} |= dtype_(size) = 3
>>
Rule 8 (batch size should be positive)
{input : tensor} |= shape(input, 0) > 0
>>
Rule 9 (height and width of input should be positive)
{input : tensor} |= shape(input, 1) > 0 ∧ shape(input, 2) > 0
>>
Rule 10 (channels of input should be positive)
{input : tensor} |= shape(input, 3) > 0
>>
Rule 11 (if normalized is true, offsets should be within [-1, 1])
{offsets : tensor, normalized: bool} |= if normalized then (min(offsets) ≥ -1 ∧ max(offsets) ≤ 1)
>>
Rule 14 (if centered is true and normalized is false, offsets should be less than height and width of the image.)
{input : tensor, offsets : tensor, centered: bool, normalized: bool} |= if centered ∧ (normalized = false) then (max(offsets) < shape(input, 1) ∧ max(offsets) < shape(input, 2))
>>
Rule 16 (if centered is true and normalized is false, offsets should be less than height and width of the image taking into account the size.)
{input : tensor, offsets : tensor, centered: bool, normalized: bool, size: tensor} |= if centered ∧ (normalized = false) then (max(offsets) + shape(size,1)/2 ≤ shape(input, 1) ∧ max(offsets) + shape(size,0)/2 <= shape(input, 2))
>>
Rule 17 (if centered is true and normalized is false, offsets should be less than height and width of the image taking into account the size.)
{input : tensor, offsets : tensor, centered: bool, normalized: bool, size: tensor} |= if centered ∧ (normalized = false) then (min(offsets) - shape(size,1)/2 >= 0 ∧ min(offsets) - shape(size,0)/2 >= 0 ∧ max(offsets) + shape(size,1)/2 <= shape(input, 1) ∧ max(offsets) + shape(size,0)/2 <= shape(input, 2))
